SORTARR - sort a numeric BASIC array ascending, in place.

Language features
  - SEED_EXPORT; a BASIC array passed by name and sorted in place
  - standard <stdlib.h> qsort and <string.h> memcpy in a seed

Try it
  DIM E(4) : E(0)=5:E(1)=2:E(2)=8:E(3)=1:E(4)=9
    SEED h%, "SORTARR.SED" : CALL h%, "E"

Build it on the machine
  grow sortarr          # -> build/SORTARR.SED
  (grow links the berry-libc from SEEDCORE.PKT for this one automatically)
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as SORTARR.SED, ready to use.

